speechtext:
That towards making good the supply granted to His Majesty on account of certain expenses of the public service for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1951, the following sums be granted out of the consolidated revenue fund of Canada, namely-
1.	The sum of $116,793,505.67, being one-twelfth of the amount of each of the items (with the exception of item 170) set forth in the main estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1951;
2.	The amount of $254,000, being one-third of the amount of items 364, 430, 497 of the said estimates;
3.	The amount of $1,441,677, being one-twelfth of the amount of items 18, 30, 94, 189, 191, 192, 193, 194, 195, 198, 199, 360, 361, 370, 384, 385, 386, 554 of the said estimates;
4.	The amount of $833,333.33, being one-third of the amount of item 635 set forth in the supplementary estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1951. as set forth in the resolution concurred in this day in committee of supply.
